## Why This Is Asked

Tests RBAC propagation and UI behavior under real-world latency in multi-tenant environments. It exercises data isolation, audit trails, and deterministic mocks for end-to-end reliability.

## Key Concepts

- RBAC propagation and eventual consistency
- Multi-tenant data isolation
- In-place UI updates without reloads
- Audit logs and actionable traces

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright skeleton for RBAC propagation test
test('RBAC propagation without reload', async ({ page }) => {
  await loginAsSuperadmin(page);
  await createTenantProject(page, 'Acme');
  await assignRole(page, 'teammate@example.com', 'viewer');
  await upgradeRole(page, 'teammate@example.com', 'editor');
  await waitForPropagation(page, 120000);
  await assertUIReflectsRole(page, 'teammate@example.com', 'editor');
  await assertAuditLogged(page, 'RoleChanged', {
    user: 'teammate@example.com',
    newRole: 'editor'
